# Realtime events (SSE) examples for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Click "Send Request" above any request. Requests are separated by ###.
#
# How the stream is opened:
#   1. POST /api/events/ticket with the JWT  -> { ticket }  (valid 30 s, works once)
#   2. GET  /api/events?ticket=<ticket>      -> a stream that stays open
#
# REST Client waits for a response to FINISH, so it can't show a live stream.
# To watch one, run "Get a ticket" and then, within 30 s, in a terminal:
#   curl -N "http://localhost:3000/api/events?ticket=<ticket>"
# Then create/edit/delete a shift: "event: shifts-changed" appears. ": ping" comes every 25 s.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@password = Test1234!

### Login (200). Saves the token for the ticket requests.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@shifthub.dev",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### HAPPY PATH
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### Get a ticket (201, { "ticket": "..." })
# @name ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/ticket
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Open the stream with that ticket (200, stays open: REST Client keeps "waiting").
### Cancel it after a few seconds. Run within 30 s of "Get a ticket".
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?ticket={{ticket.response.body.ticket}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### SHOULD FAIL
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### 401 INVALID_TICKET: the same ticket again (single use: the request above consumed it)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?ticket={{ticket.response.body.ticket}}

### 401 INVALID_TICKET: a made-up ticket (same message as used or expired)
GET {{baseUrl}}/events?ticket=not-a-real-ticket

### 400 VALIDATION_ERROR: no ticket at all
GET {{baseUrl}}/events

### 401 UNAUTHORIZED: ticket request without a JWT
POST {{baseUrl}}/events/ticket
